  "console.voice.help": "Ask what is waiting on you. To decide something, say approve or refuse and the number.",
  /*
      THE PRICE OF A SPOKEN CONVERSATION, STATED WHERE ONE STARTS, BEFORE ANYTHING
      IS SAID. §7a: every limit is stated before the customer builds on it, not
      after they pay. The number is a placeholder filled from `voiceCreditsFor` in
      `@orvay/entitlements`, so a price change cannot leave this sentence behind.
  
      SHORT ON PURPOSE (2026-10-21), and every clause is still a fact the meter
      enforces. "From when it connects": a live session is charged for the longer
      of the connected time the voice service reports and `last_seen_at -
      opened_at` (`apps/app/src/server/voice-billing.ts`, ADR-0123). "Every
      started minute counts": that span is rounded up to whole minutes, at least
      one. "Metered on their own": live text answers are delegated to the routed
      text model and recorded turns meter transcription, text and speech
      separately, and completed paid work is charged when an answer fails. The
      longer version, with the ten-minute limit and company keys, is the voice
      paragraph of `apps/docs/src/content/<locale>/plans.mdx`, which renders this
      sentence above it through `VoiceRate`. The overlay shows it before the
      microphone is asked for (`voice-entry.tsx`).
  
      THE NUMBER IS A VALUE AFTER A LABEL, never a count inside the sentence
      (§8b). "{credits} credits a minute" needs a plural rule, and French takes
      the singular below two, so a repricing to one credit would read wrong in at
      least one of six languages.
    */
