  "delegations.refused.notUndoable": "A standing approval never covers work that cannot be undone. Choose one of the listed limits.",
  "delegations.refused.spendTooSmall": "A cap on credits must be at least one hundredth of a credit.",
  "delegations.refused.proposer": "Choose an agent from the list. That one is not active in this company.",
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // THE INTEGRATION CATEGORIES.
  //
  // BOTH SURFACES READ THESE NOW, and `CATEGORY_LABEL` is gone. It was a map in
  // `@orvay/integrations` holding the English words, kept while the app's
  // integrations screen was untranslated and read it; the site already read
  // these, so a German visitor met "Development" and "Communication" as headings
  // on an otherwise German page only in the product. What was left of that map
  // when its words moved here is the ORDER of its keys, which is a fact about
  // the category set rather than about any language, and it stayed in the
  // package as `CATEGORY_ORDER`.
  //
  // Terms of art follow the department names already in each catalogue, so a
  // reader meets one word per concept across the site.
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "integrations.category.development": "Development",
  "integrations.category.revenue": "Revenue",
  "integrations.category.analytics": "Analytics",
  "integrations.category.communication": "Communication",
  "integrations.category.social": "Social",
  "integrations.category.sales": "Sales",
  "integrations.category.support": "Support",
  "integrations.category.marketing": "Marketing",
  "log.eyebrow": "The record",
  "portability.eyebrow": "Taking it with you",
  // The tail: strings that were never message ids.
  "brand.tagline": "Give your company a goal. Watch the work get done. And verified.",
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Waitlist
  //
  // Every string here is a claim made to a member of the public, so §7a applies:
  // nothing may imply the product is generally available, and the consent basis is
  // stated at the point of capture rather than buried in a policy nobody opens.
  //
  // `waitlist.consent` is stored VERBATIM on the consent record, which makes it
  // the one message in this file whose translation carries legal weight. Without
  // the exact wording a reader saw, the basis is an assertion, and an assertion is
  // what a regulator asks you to substantiate. A translated consent line is the
  // text that particular reader agreed to, so it must be recorded in the language
  // it was shown in, not resolved back to English at write time.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "company.departments.heading": "Departments",
  "company.agents.heading": "Agents",
  "company.department.legend": "New department",
  "company.department.name": "Name",
  "company.department.submit": "Add department",
  "company.department.created": "The department was added.",
  "company.department.error.short": "A department needs a name of at least two characters.",
  "company.department.error.long": "A department name is eighty characters at most.",
  "company.department.error.refused": "A gate refused this. Your policy does not allow adding a department.",
  // Ready-made teams and the department limit, 2026-10-04 (`team-catalogue.ts`, `departments.ts`).
  // English only, every key listed in TRANSLATION_DEFERRED under the same date.
  //
  // THE AUTHORITY SENTENCE IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS (§12b). A list of named agents with a purpose
